{
  // Sync-only tsconfig, read by /design-sync's esbuild bundle step (cfg.tsconfig).
  // NOT part of the app build — `tsc -b` never sees this file.
  //
  // It exists for exactly one reason: `@react-three/fiber` imports `scheduler`
  // directly (dist/events-*.esm.js), and the converter's react shim intercepts
  // every `scheduler` import with a stub that throws [SCHEDULER_MISSING] — a
  // guard aimed at design systems that leaked react-dom into their dist. Here
  // the import is legitimate (r3f's reconciler), so the throw took down the
  // whole bundle and left window.Marginalia empty.
  //
  // The converter's tsconfig-paths plugin runs BEFORE the react shim, so a
  // paths entry resolves `scheduler` to the real package first and the stub
  // never fires. Version 0.21.0 is what r3f itself declares (^0.21.0) and what
  // pnpm resolves for it at runtime, so the bundle matches the real app.
  //
  // ⚠️ This is a lockfile-derived path. If the scheduler version changes or the
  // package manager's layout changes, the build fails loudly with
  // [SCHEDULER_MISSING] again — re-point this entry. See .design-sync/NOTES.md.
  "compilerOptions": {
    "baseUrl": ".",
    "paths": {
      "scheduler": [
        "../node_modules/.pnpm/scheduler@0.21.0/node_modules/scheduler/index.js"
      ]
    }
  }
}
